# Mechanism: wgpu-measurement

command: python3 -B scripts/check-wgpu-measurement.py
inputs:
  - .cairn/mechanisms/wgpu-measurement
  - Cargo.toml
  - Cargo.lock
  - build.rs
  - src
  - crates
  - reactive-tui-macros
  - examples
  - tests
  - scripts
  - manual
  - README.md
requirements:
  - GPU-005

Reject reports missing adapter, terminal, viewport, duration, mode, achieved
frame rate, total latency, separate rendering/readback/conversion/presentation
costs, or measured quality differences. Violating fixtures must fail and the
corrected report must pass. Run the documented bounded comparison on real
hardware and explicit CPU at 60x24, 144x50, and 200x60 in an isolated Kitty
host. Capture the integrated Motion page after resizing in that same owned
host; preserve images and reports with their hashes in captured output.
Never substitute CPU fallback or software-adapter output for hardware GPU
acceptance. Presentation timing measures terminal writes, not display scanout.
The agent must inspect host images and document only the verified host setup.
